A table header whose closing brackets are missing on its line (`[[bin`, as in a half-edited
file) prints only its own line, even when the parser recovers it with the brackets of a later
header and runs its line range on to them: an outline line is always one line.
== args
input/Cargo.toml
== file input/Cargo.toml
[[bin

name = "x"
[[bin]]
name = "y"
== stdout
input/Cargo.toml (5 lines)
[L1-L5] [[bin
== stderr
== exit 0
